{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775331244-IeQFZD5lWyVx1HZOyE68","role":"assistant","created":1775331254,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see the data now. Let me look at the table structure more carefully. Looking at the 1972 data, I can see:\n\nFor 13-week Treasury bills:\n- The table shows \"Amount outstanding (millions)\" for 13-week and 26-week bills\n- Issue dates are shown in the \"13-week\" column (which seems to be the issue date)\n- The first column \"13-week\" under \"Amount outstanding (millions)\" shows the amount outstanding\n\nLooking at the 13-week bills with issue dates in February to April of 1972:\n- 2/3/72: $2,301\n- 2/10/72: $2,301\n- 2/17/72: $2,405\n- 2/25/72: $2,401\n- 3/2/72: $2,401\n- 3/9/72: $2,401\n- 3/16/72: $2,402\n- 3/23/72: $2,401\n- 3/30/72: $2,300\n- 4/6/72: $2,301\n- 4/13/72: $2,301\n- 4/20/72: $2,301\n- 4/27/72: $2,300\n\nSo for 1972, the ones exceeding 2400 million are:\n- 2/17/72: $2,405\n- 2/25/72: $2,401\n- 3/2/72: $2,401\n- 3/9/72: $2,401\n- 3/16/72: $2,402\n- 3/23/72: $2,401\n\nThat's 6 bills exceeding 2400 in 1972.\n\nWait, I need to check the data more carefully. The issue is about \"treasury security market quotations released during the last week of April\" - so for 1972, this would be the April 28, 1972 data (which is what we have in page_89.txt).\n\n\nI'll now examine the 1973 data from page_95.txt to identify the bills from February to April that exceed the 2400 million threshold.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_3b62aa445cce4f9f947bcef3","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"cat /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1973_05_page_95.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
